261
00:13:11,640 --> 00:13:14,169
I am the strongest
warrior of Drum Kingdom!

262
00:13:21,080 --> 00:13:22,460
Chesmarimo! Ha!

263
00:13:23,520 --> 00:13:24,600
Miraculous Union?

264
00:13:24,800 --> 00:13:26,388
More like Ridiculous Union.

265
00:13:26,760 --> 00:13:27,590
Sweet!

266
00:13:28,320 --> 00:13:29,620
It's Ridiculous!

267
00:13:30,200 --> 00:13:32,024
Just don't let your guard down.

268
00:13:32,500 --> 00:13:33,330
Hmm?

269
00:13:33,480 --> 00:13:35,597
They might look silly,
but don't be fooled.

270
00:13:35,680 --> 00:13:36,510
They're tough.

271
00:13:36,593 --> 00:13:39,197
So tough that the citizens
couldn't stand against them.

272
00:13:39,280 --> 00:13:42,357
That's how these thugs were
able to exile all the doctors.

273
00:13:42,440 --> 00:13:45,087
Article 1 of the Drum
Kingdom's constitution.

274
00:13:45,240 --> 00:13:48,217
Those who don't do as the king
wishes will be put to death.

275
00:13:48,300 --> 00:13:50,137
That's the number one law of this country.

276
00:13:50,220 --> 00:13:52,632
You refused my wishes and broke that law.

277
00:13:53,120 --> 00:13:56,157
Now you are all going to be
punished for your crimes.

278
00:13:56,240 --> 00:13:57,877
But first I'm going to
deal with the matter

279
00:13:57,960 --> 00:14:00,357
that quacks flack
sullying my regal castle.

280
00:14:00,440 --> 00:14:02,660
IT'S TIME I TOOK THAT THING DOWN!

281
00:14:17,980 --> 00:14:19,600
A pirate flag.

282
00:14:20,140 --> 00:14:22,480
Hey reindeer, that flag!

283
00:14:25,580 --> 00:14:29,051
Nothing is impossible for a
man who raises the pirate flag!

284
00:14:29,580 --> 00:14:31,462
Isn't that what I told you, huh?

285
00:14:41,800 --> 00:14:43,280
How dare you!

286
00:14:43,540 --> 00:14:45,980
You attacked Doctor's flag, you freak!

287
00:14:47,980 --> 00:14:49,417
Doctor tried to...

288
00:14:49,500 --> 00:14:51,440
He tried to save even you!

289
00:14:52,480 --> 00:14:53,310
Chopper,

290
00:14:54,720 --> 00:14:57,780
try not to hold a grudge
against us humans, okay?

291
00:14:59,220 --> 00:15:01,320
This country is sick right now.

292
00:15:01,880 --> 00:15:03,860
But this is Walpole, Doctor.

293
00:15:04,320 --> 00:15:07,144
Someone as bad as him
isn't worth saving, is he?

294
00:15:09,940 --> 00:15:10,770
Hmm?

295
00:15:11,560 --> 00:15:12,390
I...

296
00:15:13,580 --> 00:15:17,280
I won't hurt you if you just
leave this country forever!

297
00:15:18,460 --> 00:15:19,957
Chopper, what are you doing?

298
00:15:20,040 --> 00:15:24,177
Even if he does promise that, you
can't trust a word that desperate says!

299
00:15:24,260 --> 00:15:25,090
But...

300
00:15:26,100 --> 00:15:27,480
Doctor said... Ha!

301
00:15:30,280 --> 00:15:31,110
Chopper!

302
00:15:36,060 --> 00:15:37,480
Hey, Big Mouth!

303
00:15:40,940 --> 00:15:41,900
Straw Hat!

304
00:15:43,880 --> 00:15:47,277
You guys weren't real pirates, you
were just fake ones, weren't you?

305
00:15:47,360 --> 00:15:50,037
That's why you don't know what
flying a pirate flag means!

306
00:15:50,120 --> 00:15:53,337
Cause you were just a bunch of
fakes who didn't risk your lives!

307
00:15:53,420 --> 00:15:54,620
That guy...

308
00:15:58,720 --> 00:16:00,249
I can't take this anymore.

309
00:16:00,580 --> 00:16:01,797
Let's go up the mountain.

310
00:16:01,880 --> 00:16:03,800
Okay, Usopp? Mr. Bushido?

311
00:16:04,160 --> 00:16:06,537
The sitting around and
waiting is killing me.

312
00:16:06,620 --> 00:16:09,637
Luffy and the others could have
gotten hurt in that avalanche.

313
00:16:09,720 --> 00:16:10,657
They might be trapped.

314
00:16:10,740 --> 00:16:12,957
And don't forget, Nami had a high fever.

315
00:16:13,040 --> 00:16:14,277
Anything's happened to them.

316
00:16:14,360 --> 00:16:16,660
You're worried about Nami, and Luffy,

317
00:16:16,860 --> 00:16:20,095
and Sanji, and Dalton, and
what's going on in Alabasta.

318
00:16:23,320 --> 00:16:24,780
Vivi, can't you see it?

319
00:16:24,920 --> 00:16:26,937
You're carrying too many
burdens on your shoulders.

320
00:16:27,020 --> 00:16:27,850
Calm down.

321
00:16:29,660 --> 00:16:32,177
We don't need to go up there
at all, and do you know why?

322
00:16:32,260 --> 00:16:33,957
Because those three are fine.

323
00:16:34,040 --> 00:16:36,837
And that's Luffy and Nami and
Saint you were talking about.

324
00:16:36,920 --> 00:16:37,979
I believe in them.

325
00:16:38,700 --> 00:16:40,560
He's right. He's right.

326
00:16:43,300 --> 00:16:45,594
You have to have faith in your friends.

327
00:16:45,880 --> 00:16:48,527
Usopp does, and that's
why he can be so calm.

328
00:16:48,620 --> 00:16:49,580
I get it now.

329
00:16:50,640 --> 00:16:51,470
Thanks a lot.

330
00:16:51,640 --> 00:16:53,346
You're full of wisdom, Lusol.

331
00:16:53,460 --> 00:16:54,657
No, he's full of crap.

332
00:16:54,740 --> 00:16:56,397
He's just afraid to go up that mountain.

333
00:16:56,480 --> 00:16:57,310
Gah!

334
00:16:57,393 --> 00:16:59,997
But I heard that there were things like
yetis and huge man-eating bunnies up there!

335
00:17:00,080 --> 00:17:01,077
I don't wanna get eaten!

336
00:17:01,160 --> 00:17:03,219
Then say so from the start, coward.

337
00:17:03,380 --> 00:17:04,210
Okay!

338
00:17:04,293 --> 00:17:07,057
I don't wanna be some monster
snack, and I'm sure they're fine!

339
00:17:07,140 --> 00:17:08,787
Luffy can work out anything!

340
00:17:09,480 --> 00:17:10,800
Dalton, no! Wait!

341
00:17:14,200 --> 00:17:16,620
Hey! It's Dalton! Thank goodness!

342
00:17:16,940 --> 00:17:19,646
Would somebody please
tell me who this guy is?

343
00:17:20,460 --> 00:17:21,957
Dalton, listen to reason!

344
00:17:22,040 --> 00:17:23,877
Get out of my way!

345
00:17:23,960 --> 00:17:25,837
We can't let Wabble retake the castle.

346
00:17:25,920 --> 00:17:28,177
We just can't wait!

347
00:17:28,260 --> 00:17:29,337
You mean that's where you're heading?

348
00:17:29,420 --> 00:17:30,997
The castle in your condition?

349
00:17:31,080 --> 00:17:32,217
Are you nuts?

350
00:17:32,300 --> 00:17:35,257
My country is far more
important than my health!

351
00:17:35,340 --> 00:17:37,197
He cannot succeed!

352
00:17:37,280 --> 00:17:38,697
I will not let that happen!

353
00:17:38,780 --> 00:17:39,610
Not now!

354
00:17:39,693 --> 00:17:40,523
Not ever!

355
00:17:40,606 --> 00:17:41,436
Wabble must perish!

356
00:17:41,519 --> 00:17:45,677
But you're not strong enough to
fight them in your condition, sir!

357
00:17:45,760 --> 00:17:48,584
And the rest of us are
no match for them either.

358
00:17:49,280 --> 00:17:51,637
I'm going to settle this
thing once and for all.

359
00:17:51,720 --> 00:17:53,896
I'll stop Wapol even if it kills me.

360
00:18:10,820 --> 00:18:12,677
Here, I'll take you to the castle.

361
00:18:12,760 --> 00:18:13,590
Hop on.

362
00:18:14,840 --> 00:18:16,717
Come on now, don't be so modest.

363
00:18:16,800 --> 00:18:20,277
I just want you to save your
strength for the fight, that's all.

364
00:18:20,360 --> 00:18:21,200
Consider it.

365
00:18:23,280 --> 00:18:24,340
Just hold tight.

366
00:18:25,260 --> 00:18:26,380
Okay, here it goes.

367
00:18:27,560 --> 00:18:29,360
We'll be there in no time.

368
00:18:32,080 --> 00:18:33,300
Usopp meant well.

369
00:18:38,320 --> 00:18:40,920
Usopp, thanks, but this isn't working.

370
00:18:42,520 --> 00:18:44,240
Just give me a second, okay?

371
00:18:44,600 --> 00:18:46,117
I haven't quite hit my stride yet.

372
00:18:46,200 --> 00:18:49,717
Besides, I told you I was going to
get you to the castle and I will.

373
00:18:49,800 --> 00:18:53,682
Now that I caught my breath here,
we can get back on our very way.

374
00:18:57,080 --> 00:18:59,080
Dammit, what the hell is he doing?

375
00:19:00,800 --> 00:19:04,741
You're just going to sit there and
whine or are you coming with us?

376
00:19:05,280 --> 00:19:06,110
Zoro.

377
00:19:08,640 --> 00:19:09,880
You stupid jerk!

378
00:19:10,080 --> 00:19:11,256
You thunder stealer!

379
00:19:11,780 --> 00:19:12,720
Knock it off!

380
00:19:15,420 --> 00:19:16,840
Why did you do that?

381
00:19:17,060 --> 00:19:20,097
Just as I was getting my
second wind, too. I was.

382
00:19:20,180 --> 00:19:21,460
Sure you were. I was.

383
00:19:21,640 --> 00:19:22,597
I'll tell you what to shoot.

384
00:19:22,680 --> 00:19:25,500
I'm gonna kick you. Hey, wait. Hold up.

385
00:19:25,660 --> 00:19:28,280
There's an easier way
up to the castle. Huh?

386
00:19:29,460 --> 00:19:32,920
Instead of walking, take the
ropeway. Ropeway? Impossible.

387
00:19:33,180 --> 00:19:36,477
There hasn't been one connecting
to Wackel's castle for a while.

388
00:19:36,560 --> 00:19:39,417
Someone's obviously reconnected
one because I just saw it.

389
00:19:39,500 --> 00:19:41,437
There was a rope leading
from the castle to

390
00:19:41,520 --> 00:19:44,108
a big white tree on the
outskirts of Gyasta.

391
00:19:44,260 --> 00:19:45,090
Gyasta, huh?

392
00:19:45,320 --> 00:19:46,877
That's the name of the town that Dr.

393
00:19:46,960 --> 00:19:48,784
Kureha was headed to, remember?

394
00:19:49,420 --> 00:19:51,720
What a pirate flag means, Straw Hat!

395
00:19:53,800 --> 00:19:55,100
Don't make me laugh!

396
00:19:55,340 --> 00:19:56,720
Flags have no meaning!

397
00:19:57,060 --> 00:19:59,437
If you think that, you're
dumber than you look!

398
00:19:59,520 --> 00:20:00,350
What?

399
00:20:01,180 --> 00:20:02,010
Listen!

400
00:20:02,093 --> 00:20:03,677
Pirate flags stand for
something, Big Mouth!

401
00:20:03,760 --> 00:20:05,817
They're not raised to some kind of joke!

402
00:20:05,900 --> 00:20:06,730
Moron!

403
00:20:06,813 --> 00:20:08,977
The only joke is that I've let
you live as long as I have.

404
00:20:09,060 --> 00:20:13,295
Since you dared put that flag back,
it's time I delivered the punchline!

405
00:20:13,500 --> 00:20:15,820
Well, take your best shot, Big Mouth!

406
00:20:16,080 --> 00:20:17,660
You can't break this flag!

407
00:20:17,960 --> 00:20:20,100
The skull on it is a symbol of fate!

408
00:20:22,420 --> 00:20:23,780
Hey you, look out!

409
00:20:26,460 --> 00:20:27,290
Luffy!

410
00:20:27,440 --> 00:20:28,940
That was a direct hit!

411
00:20:32,060 --> 00:20:34,295
He and that flag were blown to pieces!

412
00:20:54,760 --> 00:20:56,700
Told you. See?

413
00:20:58,040 --> 00:20:58,870
What?

414
00:20:58,953 --> 00:20:59,783
How'd he do that?

415
00:20:59,866 --> 00:21:00,781
It's impossible.

416
00:21:01,140 --> 00:21:05,997
I have no idea who this pirate flag
originally belonged to, but it doesn't matter.

417
00:21:06,080 --> 00:21:09,260
A pirate flag is someone's
pledge to risk their life!

418
00:21:09,440 --> 00:21:12,675
It's not something to be shot
at or made fun of, jerks!

419
00:21:14,740 --> 00:21:18,677
It stands for something that you
stupid jackasses will never understand!

420
00:21:18,760 --> 00:21:20,120
Not in a million years!

421
00:21:26,880 --> 00:21:27,710
Incredible!

422
00:21:28,120 --> 00:21:30,620
So this is a pirate!

423
00:21:31,060 --> 00:21:32,220
What are pirates?

424
00:21:32,540 --> 00:21:34,237
They're dashing swashbucklers.

425
00:21:34,320 --> 00:21:36,180
It's great to be a pilot.

426
00:21:36,400 --> 00:21:38,800
The most amazing people sail the seas.

427
00:21:39,200 --> 00:21:41,640
Chopper, someday you've got to go.

428
00:21:46,940 --> 00:21:48,540
Hey reindeer! Huh?

429
00:21:48,860 --> 00:21:53,437
I'm gonna kick these guys' butts for showing
your friend's flag disrespect, you in?

430
00:21:53,520 --> 00:21:54,400
Uh, me?

431
00:21:54,820 --> 00:21:55,820
You idiot!

432
00:21:56,300 --> 00:21:58,065
You just don't get it, do you?

433
00:21:58,240 --> 00:22:01,017
Alright then, since you feel
so strongly about that flag,

434
00:22:01,100 --> 00:22:02,924
I'll destroy you along with it!

435
00:22:03,240 --> 00:22:05,200
I don't think so, tubby.

436
00:22:10,480 --> 00:22:12,480
Looks like your backbone gave out.

437
00:22:14,200 --> 00:22:17,557
Your condition will continue
to worsen if you keep moving.

438
00:22:17,640 --> 00:22:18,560
So stop!

439
00:22:19,180 --> 00:22:20,080
Doctor's order!

440
00:22:26,220 --> 00:22:30,117
If you two want to fight amongst yourselves,
then please, by all means, do so.

441
00:22:30,200 --> 00:22:34,671
but I hope you'll at least watch your
friend in that flag get blown to bits!

442
00:22:34,780 --> 00:22:35,610
Straw Hat!

443
00:22:35,693 --> 00:22:36,740
Say your prayers!

444
00:22:38,160 --> 00:22:39,200
Stop it!

445
00:22:41,360 --> 00:22:42,580
That's the spirit!

446
00:22:43,020 --> 00:22:44,740
Go get him, reindeer guy!

447
00:22:49,000 --> 00:22:50,840
Waffle, sir, watch out!

448
00:22:56,080 --> 00:22:57,137
Would you look at that?

449
00:22:57,220 --> 00:23:00,691
The little furball's got more
courage than a full-grown man

450
00:23:03,380 --> 00:23:08,204
I'm sorry Frank, but there's no way I'm
gonna let you lay a single paw on our king

451
00:23:14,280 --> 00:23:18,037
Wow there really are some strange
creatures in this world You must be that

452
00:23:18,120 --> 00:23:21,977
Yeti the villagers hated and feared they
tried to kill you and chased you away,

453
00:23:22,060 --> 00:23:22,890
right?

454
00:23:22,973 --> 00:23:26,137
I bet you spent your whole
life all alone with no friends.

455
00:23:26,220 --> 00:23:28,280
You're a monster Nobody likes you.

456
00:23:28,400 --> 00:23:31,777
People want to kill you, but here
you are trying to save this country.

457
00:23:31,860 --> 00:23:33,857
That's the stupidest
thing I've ever heard!

458
00:23:33,940 --> 00:23:34,770
Shut up!

459
00:23:34,853 --> 00:23:38,877
Even if I don't have friends, I can
stand by for something I believe in!

460
00:23:38,960 --> 00:23:42,480
And as long as the flag
flies, I will! Hey!

461
00:23:42,680 --> 00:23:43,680
That's not true!

462
00:23:44,320 --> 00:23:45,150
Huh?

463
00:23:46,840 --> 00:23:48,437
You do have friends!

464
00:23:48,520 --> 00:23:50,049
I'm your friend, reindeer!

465
00:23:50,480 --> 00:23:51,310
Me!

466
00:24:03,880 --> 00:24:05,280
Oh no, Straw Hat!

467
00:24:10,280 --> 00:24:12,162
You should be flat as a pancake!

468
00:24:12,380 --> 00:24:14,477
Yeah, but I'm fine,
because I'm a rubber man.

469
00:24:14,560 --> 00:24:15,390
Rubber?

470
00:24:16,680 --> 00:24:20,268
Hey, reindeer, can you finish
off that two-headed guy for me?

471
00:24:20,440 --> 00:24:21,616
That one over there?

472
00:24:21,760 --> 00:24:22,600
Piece of cake.

473
00:24:23,080 --> 00:24:26,580
Good, while you're doing
that, I'll take care of.

474
00:24:27,220 --> 00:24:28,050
This one!

475
00:24:29,540 --> 00:24:32,377
You dare to knock me, this
country's monarch, over?

476
00:24:32,460 --> 00:24:34,048
You'll pay for that insult!

477
00:24:34,560 --> 00:24:36,100
I'm taking you down!

478
00:24:36,640 --> 00:24:38,740
Is that so, you and what army?

479
00:24:39,440 --> 00:24:40,734
Huh, you little freak?

480
00:24:41,640 --> 00:24:44,699
Freak, that's like the pot
calling the kettle black.

481
00:24:48,180 --> 00:24:51,497
If you keep moving around, you
may lose the ability to walk?

482
00:24:51,580 --> 00:24:53,637
so just stay down there and shut up.

483
00:24:53,720 --> 00:24:58,544
And don't worry, when push comes to shove,
of my little reindeer can hold his own.

484
00:25:01,440 --> 00:25:02,300
Listen up!

485
00:25:02,440 --> 00:25:04,760
My name's Tony Tony Chopper, not Freak.

486
00:25:04,960 --> 00:25:07,784
It's a name the world's
greatest doctor gave me.

487
00:25:08,320 --> 00:25:09,940
He was a wonderful man.

488
00:25:10,260 --> 00:25:14,760
Even if he forgave you for disrespecting
his flag, I won't forgive you!

489
00:25:21,440 --> 00:25:24,264
The only one who will
show no forgiveness is me.

490
00:25:24,440 --> 00:25:25,500
I'll stomp you.

491
00:25:27,020 --> 00:25:28,580
Rumble Ball.
